<https://emsenn.net/ns/schema/glossary/terms/translation-variance-record>
    rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "translation variance record" ;
    rdfs:comment "How one Daodejing/Yijing term is rendered across published English translations, set beside this section's own house reading. One shared shape for every term in this glossary that carries a translation-variance record, rather than one near-identical JSON Schema per term: dao, de, wu-wei, ziran, pu, and daodejing all instantiate this same structure, parameterized by `term`, `hanzi`, `pinyin`, `locus`, `translations`, and `houseTranslation` — the mechanics of comparing translators do not vary by which term is being compared. Each term's own thin schema (e.g. dao.schema.json) fixes `term` and $refs this file, mirroring how functor.schema.json $refs the shared category.schema.json rather than restating category structure per functor." .

